## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Dual-screen setup**: Your design describes a separate "Voter Screen" vs "Officer Screen." In a single-browser prototype, the best approach is to open the voter confirmation screen in a **second browser window/tab** (via `window.open`) that auto-refreshes via polling. Does this work for your demo setup, or do you prefer a **single-page split view** (two panels side by side)?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Receipt privacy**: As you noted, a receipt showing the actual candidate choice is a privacy/coercion risk in real elections. For your prototype, should I include the candidate name on the receipt, or show only "Vote Successfully Recorded" + Receipt ID? (The plan defaults to showing the candidate name since this is a college prototype, with a clearly visible "SIMULATION" watermark.)

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Countdown timer**: The voter has 30 seconds to review before the session auto-cancels and returns to search. Should this auto-cancel behavior be included, or should the session wait indefinitely until the voter acts?

