## Proposed Changes

### Backend — New Model

#### [NEW] VoteAuditLog.js
`server/models/VoteAuditLog.js`

New Mongoose model tracking every officer action per voter session:
- `officerId`, `voterId`, `electionId`
- `sessionId` (UUID for grouping one voter's full flow)
- `events[]` — array of `{ action, candidateId, timestamp }` where action is one of: `session_started`, `candidate_selected`, `voter_requested_change`, `candidate_reselected`, `voter_confirmed`
- `finalCandidateId`, `status` (`pending` | `confirmed` | `abandoned`)
- `receiptId` (UUID like `VOTE-8F29A71C`)

---

### Backend — Officer Controller

#### [MODIFY] officer.controller.js
`server/controllers/officer.controller.js`

Add 4 new controller functions:

| Function | Route | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `startVoteSession` | `POST /officer/session/start` | Creates a pending VoteAuditLog entry, returns `sessionId` |
| `selectCandidate` | `POST /officer/session/select` | Updates session with selected candidate, appends audit event |
| `getSessionStatus` | `GET /officer/session/:sessionId` | Voter screen polls this to see current state |
| `voterConfirmVote` | `POST /officer/session/confirm` | **Voter-only** — locks the vote, creates Vote record, generates receipt |
| `voterRequestChange` | `POST /officer/session/change` | Voter requests change, appends event, resets status to `pending_selection` |
| `getOfficerAuditStats` | `GET /admin/officer-audit` | Returns per-officer stats: votes handled, change count, change rate, flagged if >15% |

The existing `castOfflineVote` function is **kept** (for backward compatibility) but the new flow uses the session-based approach.

